{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And from the hand of a foreigner you shall not offer.</b> Even though we accept vows and freewill offerings from them, we do not accept from them animals with blemishes, even those produced by castration — even though castrated animals are considered excellent among them, and there is no concern of ״הַקְרִיבֵהוּ נָא לְפֶחָתֶךָ״ (Malachi 1:8) in this. The reason is that the castrated animal is unfit for the altar." "<b>Because their corruption is in them, a blemish is in them.</b> For even though it is a hidden blemish, it corrupts them from their intended perfection — which is the capacity to reproduce its own kind."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:20.413132437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}